      "text": "Biological materials",
      "level": 2,
      "attributes": "#biological-materials toc=\"Biological materials\"",
      "_template": "heading"
    },
    {
      "body": "<p>This section documents the biological materials and experimental methods used in wet-lab work. Deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) and ribonucleic acid are the nucleic acids represented in the sequence entries. We summarize the designed single-guide ribonucleic acid sequences, constructed plasmids and engineered strains generated in our project. Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) underpins the cloning workflows described below. The chassis species is <em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em>; <em>Escherichia coli</em> (<em>E. coli</em>) is used for plasmid propagation.</p>",
      "_template": "text"
    },
